      plain: 'Puts rows in order, and TOP keeps just the first few.',
      lesson: 'ORDER BY decides the order rows come out in; add DESC for biggest or newest first. TOP (n) right after SELECT keeps only the first n rows. SQL Server reads a query as FROM, then WHERE, then SELECT, then ORDER BY, which is why ORDER BY can use the friendly names you made with AS.',
