      lesson: 'DML changes the rows inside a table. INSERT adds new rows, UPDATE changes values, DELETE removes rows. UPDATE and DELETE without a WHERE touch every single row, so the safe habit is: preview with SELECT, change with a key-based WHERE, then check again.',
