      plain: 'Keeps only the rows that pass a test.',
      lesson: 'WHERE looks at each row one at a time and asks a yes-or-no question: is this product over $40? Is this customer active? AND means both must be true, OR means either. When you mix them, parentheses say which parts belong together.',
      analogy: 'Going through a shoebox of receipts and keeping only the ones over $40.',
      kind: 'WHERE is the everyday filter, so it’s a very natural first reach.',
