      plain: 'Keeps every row from the first table, match or not. Great for finding what’s missing.',
      lesson: 'LEFT JOIN keeps everything from the first table. Rows with no match get empty (NULL) boxes from the second table, so adding WHERE b.key IS NULL finds the gaps: who never ordered, what never sold. When chaining three tables, say what one output row is before you count, or the totals can multiply.',
      analogy: 'Taking attendance from the full class list. Everyone stays on the list; absent kids just have an empty box by their name.',
